1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,080
kapag tomatak buka habang nag-ve-video gamit ang phone mo,

2
00:00:03,580 --> 00:00:06,760
bakit hindi masakit sa mata o para ang lumilindol ang footage.

3
00:00:07,380 --> 00:00:09,420
Kung titignan mo ang loob ng camera module,

4
00:00:09,920 --> 00:00:11,680
may physical suspension system,

5
00:00:11,960 --> 00:00:16,720
at matinding algorithm na nagtutulungan para ang mukhang lumulutang ang camera mo.

6
00:00:17,280 --> 00:00:19,100
Paano ko maghana ang OIS,

7
00:00:19,560 --> 00:00:21,300
o optical image stabilization.

8
00:00:21,880 --> 00:00:23,160
Sa loob ng camera bump,

9
00:00:23,560 --> 00:00:25,240
hindi nakadikit ng dyrecho ang lens.

10
00:00:25,240 --> 00:00:35,160
Sa tuto lang lumulutang ito sa Microscopic Suspension Springs at napapalibutan ng 4-pole voice coil electromagnets o VCM's.

11
00:00:35,560 --> 00:00:43,540
Kapag gumalog ang kamay mo, agad itong nararamdaman ng Microscopic MEMS gyroscope sa bilis na 1000 times per second.

12
00:00:43,940 --> 00:00:49,140
Kung tumagilit ang phone, pakanan, agad hihilain ng electromagnets ang lens pakaliwa.

13
00:00:49,640 --> 00:00:52,680
Pisikalitong kinakan sila ang pagalog sa bilis ng liwanag.

14
00:00:52,680 --> 00:01:02,460
Sa mga bagong flagship tulad ng iPhone hindi lang lens ang gumagalau, sensor shift OIS ang gamit kung saan mismong CMOS sensor ang lumulutang.

15
00:01:03,040 --> 00:01:09,180
Pero may limitation ang OIS, kaya lang nito mag compensate ng hanggang isa o dalawang degrees ng tilt.

16
00:01:09,580 --> 00:01:18,300
Kapag tumatak buka o tumatalon ko lang ang physical movement ng magnets, dito na papasok ang EIS o Electronic Image Stabilization.

17
00:01:18,300 --> 00:01:28,920
Ang EIS ay puroong software at math. Sa halit nagamitin ang buong 4K sensor, makakrop ang phone ng 10-20% buffer margins sa paligit ng video.

18
00:01:29,420 --> 00:01:33,080
Isipin mo na may virtual camera window sa loob ng mas malaking canvas.

19
00:01:33,800 --> 00:01:41,180
Gamit ang gyro data at frame-by-frame motion vector analysis hino hulaan ang algorithm kung saan gagalaw ang susunud na frame.

20
00:01:41,180 --> 00:01:45,040
Ini-Shift at winawarp niito ang virtual window pixel-by-pixel

21
00:01:45,040 --> 00:01:47,020
para mag-mukang steady ang horizon

22
00:01:47,020 --> 00:01:48,660
kaid nagtatal bugang phone mo.

23
00:01:49,120 --> 00:01:51,460
Kapag pinagsama ang OIS at EIS

24
00:01:51,460 --> 00:01:54,860
tinatawag itong hybrid stabilization o action mode

25
00:01:54,860 --> 00:01:57,380
smooth na cinematic glide ang resulta

26
00:01:57,380 --> 00:01:58,960
kaid mag sprint kasahagdan.

27
00:01:59,480 --> 00:02:01,040
Pero may trade-off ito

28
00:02:01,040 --> 00:02:02,580
dahil nakakrop ang sensor

29
00:02:02,580 --> 00:02:04,460
at kelangan ng mobilis na shutter speed

30
00:02:04,460 --> 00:02:05,920
para maawasa ng motion blur

31
00:02:05,920 --> 00:02:09,060
madilim at grainy ang EIS video sa gabi.

32
00:02:09,060 --> 00:02:13,660
Kaya salo-light madalas nanginginig o nagiging jelly ang video,

33
00:02:14,060 --> 00:02:15,600
dahil nag-istragalang algorithm.

34
00:02:16,320 --> 00:02:17,960
Kaya, ito ang tanong kasainyo.

35
00:02:18,480 --> 00:02:20,820
Naranasan mo nubang mag-video habang tumatakbo,

36
00:02:21,060 --> 00:02:24,480
at napan sinmubang pagkakaiba ng may OIS sa wala,

37
00:02:24,940 --> 00:02:25,940
ikamit mo sababa.

38
00:02:26,440 --> 00:02:27,780
Follow me for more Tech Explained.

39
00:02:28,280 --> 00:02:28,560
See ya!
